turtle/simple - Logo-style turtle graphics

A simple turtle graphics module with implicit state. Call new(dim) to start drawing.

Logical space is 200x200 by default (range -100 to +100). The dim parameter sets pixel window size; logical coordinates scale accordingly.

===

new(dim)

Create a dim x dim pixel canvas and turtle at center. The window appears when you call this. If you close the window, call new() again to start a fresh session.

Example:
    use("turtle/simple")
    new(800)
    forward(50)

===

logical(size)

Set logical space to size x size. Rescales coordinate mapping. Default is 200.

Example:
    logical(100)  # range now -50 to +50

===

forward(distance)

Move the turtle forward by the given distance in logical units. Draws a line if the pen is down. Position is clamped to bounds.

Example:
    forward(50)

===

backward(distance)

Move the turtle backward by the given distance. Equivalent to forward(-distance).

Example:
    backward(25)

===

left(angle)

Turn the turtle left by the given angle in degrees.

Example:
    left(90)

===

right(angle)

Turn the turtle right by the given angle in degrees.

Example:
    right(45)

===

pen_up()

Lift the pen. Subsequent movements will not draw lines.

Example:
    pen_up()
    forward(50)
    pen_down()

===

pen_down()

Lower the pen. Subsequent movements will draw lines.

===

pen_size(n)

Set pen width to n logical units. Minimum 1 pixel.

Example:
    pen_size(2)
    forward(50)

===

set_color(color)

Set the pen and turtle color. Use a symbol like :white, :red, :green, :blue, :cyan, :yellow, :magenta.

Example:
    set_color(:red)
    forward(50)

===

show_turtle()

Show the turtle marker.

===

hide_turtle()

Hide the turtle marker.

===

home()

Move to center without drawing, reset heading to 0.

===

clear()

Clear the canvas. Does not move the turtle.

===

position()

Return the turtle's current position as [@point, x, y] in logical coordinates. Center is [0, 0].

===

heading()

Return the turtle's current heading in degrees. 0 = north, 90 = east, 180 = south, 270 = west.

===

Example: Draw a square

    use("turtle/simple")
    new(800)
    
    forward(50)
    right(90)
    forward(50)
    right(90)
    forward(50)
    right(90)
    forward(50)
